WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:03.594
Deputy Cleo sure was proud of herself.

2
00:00:03.595 --> 00:00:10.091
The sun was still rising, and she was heading to work!

3
00:00:10.092 --> 00:00:14.866
But when she got to the sheriff's office, she sighed.

4
00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:19.778
Roscoe was already there, sitting outside.

5
00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:23.653
"Why are you here so early?" she asked.

6
00:00:23.654 --> 00:00:27.994
"New folks arrive by train every morning," Roscoe said.

7
00:00:27.995 --> 00:00:31.098
"I like to see who's coming into Prickly Pear."

8
00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:36.238
Cleo took a seat beside him and yawned.

9
00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:40.645
She soon heard the train arriving.

10
00:00:40.646 --> 00:00:45.274
A few minutes later, folks from the train started walking by.

11
00:00:45.275 --> 00:00:48.355
Most carried bags.

12
00:00:48.356 --> 00:00:54.396
"I don't see any trouble." Cleo yawned again.

13
00:00:54.397 --> 00:00:57.288
"Maybe I'll take a nap."

14
00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:00.825
That's when Cleo saw a pair of cats.

15
00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:04.612
One was carrying a big trunk.

16
00:01:04.613 --> 00:01:07.810
"That looks heavy," Cleo thought.

17
00:01:07.811 --> 00:01:11.351
Cleo went over to the new cat.

18
00:01:11.352 --> 00:01:13.680
"Let me help you with that."

19
00:01:13.681 --> 00:01:16.010
The cat looked startled.

20
00:01:16.011 --> 00:01:20.247
"No, thanks. I can handle it."

21
00:01:20.248 --> 00:01:23.103
"It's no trouble," Cleo said.

22
00:01:23.104 --> 00:01:25.656
"What brings you to Prickly Pear?"

23
00:01:25.657 --> 00:01:28.723
The other cat took out a silk fan.

24
00:01:28.724 --> 00:01:32.170
She opened it and fanned herself.

25
00:01:32.171 --> 00:01:36.492
"We've always wanted to see the West," she said.

26
00:01:36.493 --> 00:01:41.880
"It's so big! My name is Sasha and this is Violet."

27
00:01:41.881 --> 00:01:47.999
"Howdy!" Cleo said. "I'm Deputy Cleo, and that's Sheriff Roscoe."

28
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.096
Roscoe tipped his hat.

29
00:01:51.097 --> 00:01:55.865
"We're looking for a place to stay," Violet said.

30
00:01:55.866 --> 00:01:58.670
Cleo pointed down the street.

31
00:01:58.671 --> 00:02:01.031
"You just passed the boardinghouse.

32
00:02:01.032 --> 00:02:03.691
Why don't you leave your trunk there?

33
00:02:03.692 --> 00:02:05.837
Then I'll join you for a drink.

34
00:02:05.838 --> 00:02:08.903
There's a juice saloon across the street."

35
00:02:08.904 --> 00:02:14.812
Violet looked nervous. "Oh, I don't know . . ."

36
00:02:14.813 --> 00:02:18.360
"It's okay, Violet," Sasha said.

37
00:02:18.361 --> 00:02:23.048
"No one will steal our trunk with Deputy Cleo around."

38
00:02:23.049 --> 00:02:34.299
Cleo waved to Roscoe. "I'll be back soon."

39
00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:39.126
A little while later, the three cats were sitting in the saloon.

40
00:02:39.127 --> 00:02:42.391
Cleo had just finished telling a story.

41
00:02:42.392 --> 00:02:46.840
"And that's how we caught the gang," she said.

42
00:02:46.841 --> 00:02:53.333
"You're so brave!" Sasha said. "And smart!"

43
00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:59.398
"Yeah," Violet said. "You should be the sheriff!"

44
00:02:59.399 --> 00:03:03.472
Well, that made Cleo feel special.

45
00:03:03.473 --> 00:03:06.785
"I like these cats!" she thought.

46
00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:11.183
Then she stood up. "I should get back to work."

47
00:03:11.184 --> 00:03:14.071
"Bye, now," Violet said.

48
00:03:14.072 --> 00:03:20.411
Sasha waved. "Thanks again."

49
00:03:20.412 --> 00:03:26.387
Back at the sheriff's office, Cleo found Roscoe frowning over a telegram.

50
00:03:26.388 --> 00:03:30.152
"What's wrong?" she asked.

51
00:03:30.153 --> 00:03:33.098
He put the telegram down.

52
00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:36.928
"Thieves robbed a jewelry store in Plattsville last night."

53
00:03:36.929 --> 00:03:39.677
Cleo rubbed her chin.

54
00:03:39.678 --> 00:03:42.736
"That's two train stops from here."

55
00:03:42.737 --> 00:03:45.267
"Right," Roscoe said.

56
00:03:45.268 --> 00:03:53.923
"Which means the thieves probably boarded the train—to Prickly Pear!"

